WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:10.456
- I've been threatened by
Haiti with voodoo over food;

00:00:10.456 --> 00:00:13.892
I've taken mangoes from
passengers from Jamaica,

00:00:13.892 --> 00:00:15.768
and been threatened with my life.

00:00:15.768 --> 00:00:17.984
Never a dull moment here at JFK.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.372
Make it easier, that's it.

00:00:20.372 --> 00:00:23.785
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.785 --> 00:00:25.984
The reason why we're
confiscating all this stuff

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:28.847
is not because it's
harmful to the human being.

00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:31.537
It's harmful for our
plants and our animals.

00:00:31.537 --> 00:00:32.964
This is a big port.

00:00:32.964 --> 00:00:36.345
Last month we processed
1.5 million passengers.

00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:37.647
You figure between fruits and vegetables,

00:00:37.647 --> 00:00:40.404
you're talking about two or
three hundred kilos a day

00:00:40.404 --> 00:00:41.481
in just one terminal.

00:00:41.481 --> 00:00:44.393
So you're talking about
four to six hundred pounds.

00:00:44.393 --> 00:00:46.505
- [Interviewer] What kind of
foods are you confiscating?

00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:47.585
- Every day is different,

00:00:47.585 --> 00:00:48.947
every season is different,

00:00:48.947 --> 00:00:52.053
Chinese New Year, Christmas, Easter.

00:00:52.053 --> 00:00:54.524
We have beef candy from China,

00:00:54.524 --> 00:00:56.566
Serrano ham from Spain,

00:00:56.566 --> 00:00:57.766
we have lots of avocados,

00:00:57.766 --> 00:00:59.566
salami from Italy,

00:00:59.566 --> 00:01:02.045
no Pedro, I take it back, salami supremo,

00:01:02.045 --> 00:01:03.545
that's Spain also.

00:01:05.025 --> 00:01:06.622
Once the food item is seized,

00:01:06.622 --> 00:01:08.622
it's put in what we
call the contraband bin.

00:01:08.622 --> 00:01:10.787
We drag the contraband
bin across the terminal.

00:01:10.787 --> 00:01:12.025
It's about a block long,

00:01:12.025 --> 00:01:13.039
get a little exercise

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.076
and begin the process of grinding up

00:01:15.076 --> 00:01:16.947
all the prohibited food items.

00:01:16.947 --> 00:01:19.197
We're at the grinder table.

00:01:20.034 --> 00:01:21.742
The officer will look

00:01:21.742 --> 00:01:24.425
and see if there's any little
exit holes or entry holes,

00:01:24.425 --> 00:01:26.825
and that's where you're
gonna find the insect.

00:01:26.825 --> 00:01:28.562
- [Interviewer] Do you enjoy
that part of the process?

00:01:28.562 --> 00:01:30.366
Is it kind of a stress reliever for you?

00:01:30.366 --> 00:01:32.046
- Oh, the grinder is great.

00:01:32.046 --> 00:01:34.483
Sometimes I go home with a
little bit of mango juice

00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:36.327
and passion fruit juice on.

00:01:36.327 --> 00:01:37.305
You're just having fun,

00:01:37.305 --> 00:01:38.723
the water's splashing in your face,

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:40.867
but this is what we have to do

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.596
to protect American agriculture,

00:01:42.596 --> 00:01:44.346
it's part of our job.

